  X. THE 6 = 2*3 FACTORIZATION IN SKIP SPACE
  --------------------------------------------------

  Skip lengths: 2, 3, 4, 5
  2 = first prime (parity)
  3 = second prime (curvature)
  4 = 2*2 (double parity)
  5 = path length - 1

  3-cycle skip compositions (s1+s2=s3):
  (1,1,2): uses path arcs — NOT in tiling (path fixed)
  (1,2,3): one path + one skip-2 + one skip-3
  (1,3,4): one path + one skip-3 + one skip-4
  (1,4,5): one path + one skip-4 + one skip-5
  (2,1,3): one skip-2 + one path + one skip-3
  (2,2,4): two skip-2 + one skip-4
  (2,3,5): one skip-2 + one skip-3 + one skip-5
  (3,1,4): one skip-3 + one path + one skip-4
  (3,2,5): one skip-3 + one skip-2 + one skip-5

  KEY PATTERN: The 3-cycle {i, i+2, i+5} uses skips (2,3,5).
  2+3=5, and {2,3,5} are the first three primes!
  This is the 'spherical' triangle of our grand trichotomy.

  The 3-cycle {i, i+2, i+4} uses skips (2,2,4).
  This is the 'parity-doubled' triangle (purely INERT).

  The 3-cycle {i, i+1, i+3} uses skips (1,2,3).
  This includes a path arc (skip 1) — the 'path-anchored' triangle.

  Contribution of each skip-triple to total c3:
    (1,1,2):   2048 / 6144 = 33.3%
    (1,2,3):    768 / 6144 = 12.5%
    (1,3,4):    512 / 6144 = 8.3%
    (1,4,5):    256 / 6144 = 4.2%
    (2,1,3):    768 / 6144 = 12.5%
    (2,2,4):    512 / 6144 = 8.3%
    (2,3,5):    256 / 6144 = 4.2%
    (3,1,4):    512 / 6144 = 8.3%
    (3,2,5):    256 / 6144 = 4.2%
    (4,1,5):    256 / 6144 = 4.2%

